/// Hints to the optimizer, for benchmarks.
///
/// Release builds optimize the whole program at once (D99), so a loop whose result is only
/// summed can be moved out from between two readings of the clock, or computed when the program
/// is built. `black_box` stops that.
module std.hint

/// Gives back `x`, in a way the optimizer can't see through: it can't know the result, so it
/// can't compute what depends on it in advance, and it must have `x` ready by this call, so it
/// can't drop the work that made `x` or move it past the call. It costs about one store.
pub fn black_box<T>(x: own T) -> T {
    return x
}
